# Stow ignore list for the shared herdr-app package (stow itself never links
# this file). A package-local list REPLACES stow's built-in one, so the
# built-in entries that could ever occur here are repeated at the bottom.

# settings.json is per-OS, in home/herdr-app-darwin and home/herdr-app-linux:
# everything else in Herdr's config dir is shared, this one file is not.
# Never let this package own it. Herdr's saves, and on the macs the activation
# settings merge, write through a dangling settings.json link, so a pull that
# moves the file under a running Herdr recreates it here. Linked from here, it
# would conflict with the per-OS package and stow would skip this whole
# package (keys, layouts, mods, themes) on that machine.
^/\.config/herdr-app/settings\.json

# From stow's built-in list.
\.git
\.gitignore
\.\#.+
.+~
\#.*\#
